WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.580
So, it turns out Thanos wasn't wrong when
he declared that there would be "no resurrections

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.680
this time" for Loki.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.220
Still, that doesn't mean much where Infinity
Stones and trickster gods are concerned; Loki

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.580
manages something in Endgame with potentially
huge ramifications.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.780
Spoilers from here on out!

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.260
Quick recap: When the Avengers go back in
time to get the Infinity Stones in Endgame,

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:23.669
one team heads to Stark Tower just after the
team has captured Loki in Avengers.

00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:27.400
In part because of the interference of the
Avengers from the future, the captive Loki

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:30.699
gets his hands on the Tesseract and disappears
in a blue flash.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.440
The big question is, where did he go?

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:36.680
The most immediate concern about Loki is whether
or not he creates an alternate timeline, split

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.100
off from the main MCU continuity, in which
he escapes the Avengers with the Tesseract.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.060
When Captain America brings all the Stones
back to their respective times, does he return

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.960
everything to normal and stop any timelines
from branching?

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.860
Or is Loki still out there with the 2012 Tesseract?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.660
If Loki does create an alternate timeline
when he escapes, and it still exists, then

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.060
that opens a whole world of possibilities.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.499
Free from the Avengers and in possession of
the Space Stone, there's no limit to where

00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:02.590
Loki might go.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.160
He might bring the Tesseract to his benefactor
Thanos.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:09.640
The Mad Titan's emissary, the Other, makes
it perfectly clear what Loki risks if he fails

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.460
Thanos, and none of it is pleasant.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:18.760
"There will be no realm, no barren moon, no
crevice where he can not find you."

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.860
With the Chitauri forces Thanos gave to Loki
destroyed, the God of Mischief might see getting

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:26.900
the Tesseract back to the Titan as the only
way to save his life

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.800
However, Thanos probably wouldn't be Loki's
first stop.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.540
Losing the Chitauri forces to the Avengers
would not necessarily sign Loki's death warrant.

00:01:34.549 --> 00:01:37.930
But there's something we know now that we
didn't know when Avengers was released, that

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.940
Thanos gave Loki an Infinity Stone to get
an Infinity Stone.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.800
He trusted the Mind Stone to Loki, and in
Endgame Loki leaves it behind when he escapes.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.220
How does it help Thanos' plans if he gains
one Stone just to lose another?

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.920
Unless Loki is uncharacteristically foolish,
he won't run to Thanos.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.440
Doing so would just get his neck broken six
years early.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.600
Whatever deal was struck between Thanos and
Loki, it all happens off-screen.

00:01:59.609 --> 00:02:03.520
We don't know the extent of Loki's knowledge
regarding Thanos, his plans, and his other

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.020
allies.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.600
When Thor confronts Loki in Avengers, Loki
tells his brother he knows all about the Tesseract.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.440
"I have seen worlds you've never known about.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.700
I have grown, Odinson, in my exile.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.140
I have seen the true power of the Tesseract."

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.560
So unless he's lying, he knows quite a bit.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:25.470
If we assume by 2012 that Thanos and Ronan
the Accuser are already allies, and that Loki

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.380
knows about the alliance, Ronan could be Loki's
first stop.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.820
At that point, Ronan is in no position to
challenge Thanos, and that's because he doesn't

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.260
know what Thanos is after.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.240
When Thanos tasks the Kree with capturing
the Orb, Ronan doesn't know it contains the

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:38.880
Power Stone.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.200
If Loki knows more about Thanos' machinations
than Ronan, then he has much to offer the

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.700
Kree warlord and a potential ally to protect
him from Thanos' wrath.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.580
In the now classic mid-credits scene of Avengers
when Thanos is first revealed, the Other is

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.360
warning the Mad Titan against any further
action on Earth.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.180
He tells his master that to challenge Earth
is to "court death."

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.240
If Loki guesses at this apprehension on the
part of Thanos' underlings to mess with Earth,

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.600
then the trickster might decide the best place
to be is right on Earth.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:08.460
As long as he stays under the radar of the
Avengers, he could remain on Earth for as

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:13.150
long as he wants, with his own superhero enemies
acting as a shield against Thanos' wrath.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:17.260
Or, alternatively, he could stay on Earth
with the intention of recapturing his scepter

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.280
to give it to Thanos.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:22.740
Loki probably knows if he returns to Thanos
without both Infinity Stones, the Mad Titan

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.800
will do a lot worse to him than the Hulk ever
would.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.300
In 2012, Loki's greatest weakness is his passion
for revenge.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:40.140
With an Infinity Stone at his command and
his knowledge of the secret ways into and

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:44.560
out of Asgard, his first trip after Endgame
might be back home to claim what he sees as

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.160
his rightful throne.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:50.000
In the proper MCU timeline, he doesn't have
to worry about Thanos; Loki's failure to conquer

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.480
Earth leads him straight to an Asgardian dungeon.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.540
As soon as he escapes in Thor: The Dark World,
he fakes his own death and disguises himself

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:57.080
as Odin.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:01.320
The disguise allows him to rule Asgard, yes,
but it has the added bonus of hiding him from

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.000
Thanos.

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:05.780
What's easier than conquering a world ruled
by your adoptive family?

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.780
Conquering a world ruled by no one, of course.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.520
After 2011's Thor, we don't hear much from
Jotunheim, the land of the Frost Giants.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:17.980
Thor and Malekith visit it briefly and involuntarily
during their battle in 2013's Thor: The Dark

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.680
World, but we don't exactly get a good picture
of the political situation there.

00:04:21.689 --> 00:04:25.979
We know after initially offering to help assassinate
Odin, Loki betrays and murders his biological

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.980
father, and then he attempts to use the bifrost
to destroy the frost giants' world.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.380
"It was just a bit of fun really."

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:36.680
So, when Loki escapes the Avengers in Endgame
and needs a place to hang his horned hat,

00:04:36.689 --> 00:04:40.849
a potentially leaderless Jotunheim might be
the perfect choice, and the throne could be

00:04:40.849 --> 00:04:41.580
his for the taking.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.500
He is the biological son of their dead king,
and he has an Infinity Stone to back up his

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:46.000
claim.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.900
Not to mention that with intimate knowledge
of Asgard and its most powerful leaders, he's

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:54.440
in a unique position to satisfy any frost
giants hungry to make war on Odin once more.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:59.120
The mid-credits scene of Thor: The Dark World
sees Sif and Volstagg sent to Knowhere to

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.800
deliver the Aether to the Collector.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.150
It's one of the most deceptively important
moments in the MCU, because of this line:

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.460
"The Tesseract is already on Asgard.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.340
It's unwise to keep two infinity stones so
close together."

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:16.080
Without some as-of-yet unrevealed connection
between Loki and the Collector, it's a moment

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.400
that doesn't make much sense.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:21.659
It's Loki disguised as Odin who sends the
Aether to Knowhere, and the power hungry Loki

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.560
is not someone we expect to send an Infinity
Stone to someone else.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.340
Not unless there's a plan behind it all.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:30.460
A connection between the Collector and Loki
could also explain the Grandmaster's friendship

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.099
with the trickster in Thor: Ragnarok, as Grandmaster
and the Collector are brothers.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.919
If this connection between the Collector and
Loki ever proves to be more than speculation,

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:41.160
then it could be that Knowhere was Loki's
first stop after Endgame.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.200
Although, granted, that's one of the least
likely outcomes.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:48.780
One thing that's easy to forget about Loki
is that, before Thanos finally rounds them

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:53.039
up in Avengers: Infinity War, Loki has more
encounters with more Infinity Stones than

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.200
anyone in the MCU.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.700
In Avengers, he possesses both the Mind Stone
and the Tesseract.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:02.199
After usurping Odin at the end of Thor: The
Dark World, he has access to the Reality Stone

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:06.080
until he sends it to Knowhere, and has as
much access as he wants to the Space Stone.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:09.360
Loki knows the Infinity Stones, at least,
he knows something about them.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:13.349
We don't know how much, if anything, Thanos
tells him about them, but the trickster god

00:06:13.349 --> 00:06:15.820
has a way of getting information whether you
want him to or not.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:19.720
Armed with the Infinity Stone that has the
power to bring him anywhere, Loki may decide

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.780
to go on an Infinity Stone quest of his own.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:26.091
Not only would the completion of such an endeavor
feed his hunger for power, but again, would

00:06:26.091 --> 00:06:30.320
provide him with the muscle to destroy Thanos
should the Titan come for his vengeance.

